<SubSection title="Convection" id="Convection">
<p> Convective mass transfer refers to the movement of mass through a medium as a result of the net motion of a material in the medium. It is an added effect of bulk flow on top of diffusion or dispersion, and is studied the same way as convective heat transfer. </p>
</SubSection>

<SubSubSection title="Convection-Diffusion Over a Surface" id="ConvectionDiffusion">
<p>Convection-diffusion mass transfer over a surface is analogous to convective heat transfer. The mass flow rate from 1 to 2 is:</p>
	<DisplayEquation equation="N_{A_{1-2}} = h_{m} A (c_{1} - c_{2})" title="Convective Mass Transfer" background="True"/>
where
<Itemize>
	<Item><InlineEquation equation="N_{A_{1-2}}" /> = mass flow rate from 1 to 2 <InlineEquation equation="\\left[\\frac{kg}{s}\\right]" /></Item>
	<Item><InlineEquation equation="h_{m}" /> = convective mass transfer coefficient <InlineEquation equation="\\left[\\frac{m}{s}\\right]" /></Item>
	<Item><InlineEquation equation="A" /> = area normal to flow <InlineEquation equation="[m^{2}]" /></Item>
	<Item><InlineEquation equation="c_{1}" /> = concentration of A in the fluid at the surface (not solid) <InlineEquation equation="\\left[\\frac{kg}{m^{3}}\\right]" /></Item>
	<Item><InlineEquation equation="c_{2}" /> = concentration of A in the bulk fluid <InlineEquation equation="\\left[\\frac{kg}{m^{3}}\\right]" /></Item>
</Itemize>
</SubSubSection>

